# 103. ACCEPTANCE — POSTGRESQL

-  one canonical DB runtime
-  ORM uses PostgreSQL through canonical ownership
-  transactions verified
-  migration strategy documented
-  readiness detects DB failure
-  graceful shutdown closes pool
-  no duplicate uncontrolled connection pool

---

# 104. ACCEPTANCE — VALKEY

-  Valkey has at least one intentional platform responsibility or is explicitly optional/unintegrated
-  canonical adapter exists if used
-  domain packages do not instantiate Valkey directly
-  TTL behavior tested
-  failure semantics documented
-  rate limiting uses shared backing if multi-instance support requires it
-  cache keys are namespaced
-  authorization correctness does not depend on stale indefinite cache

---

# 105. ACCEPTANCE — MINIO

-  storage API exists
