# 117. START NOW

Do not answer with another theoretical architecture document only.

Begin with actual repository inspection.

Reverify every historical finding.

Map every infrastructure service to its real consumer.

Identify all phantom/unconnected services.

Fix the highest-priority P0 first.

Then progressively consolidate the runtime and infrastructure.

Run tests after coherent changes.

Update documentation alongside implementation.

Do not claim an infrastructure service is integrated until data can demonstrably flow from Moon Server to that service.

For V3 observability specifically, prove both paths: Moon Server `/metrics` → Alloy → VictoriaMetrics, and Moon Server structured logs → Alloy → Loki.

Validate the final Compose with `docker compose config`, run the stack where the environment permits, and capture `docker stats --no-stream` plus `docker system df` as evidence of actual resource usage.

Do not claim completion prematurely.